{
  "title": "setBfree Organ",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Hammond B3 tonewheel",
        "organ. 91 tonewheels,",
        "9 drawbars, scanner",
        "vibrato, percussion,",
        "tube overdrive and a",
        "Leslie cabinet.",
        "",
        "Engine: setBfree by",
        "Robin Gareus and",
        "Fredrik Kilander.",
        "",
        "The organ takes about",
        "a second to build on",
        "load. It is silent",
        "until then. The RDY",
        "readout on Output",
        "shows 1 when it is",
        "ready to play."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Drawbars",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "How they work",
          "lines": [
            "Each drawbar adds one",
            "harmonic to every key",
            "you play. They are",
            "additive: pull more",
            "out for more of that",
            "harmonic.",
            "",
            "Range is 0 to 8.",
            "0 = fully in, silent.",
            "8 = fully out, loud.",
            "",
            "On a real B3 the tabs",
            "are numbered 0-8 too,",
            "so the numbers here",
            "match the hardware."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "The nine bars",
          "lines": [
            "0  16'   sub octave",
            "1  5 1/3 sub third",
            "2  8'    fundamental",
            "3  4'    octave",
            "4  2 2/3 twelfth",
            "5  2'    fifteenth",
            "6  1 3/5 seventeenth",
            "7  1 1/3 nineteenth",
            "8  1'    twentysecond",
            "",
            "Bars 0 and 1 are the",
            "brown ones, 2 to 5",
            "white, 6 to 8 black.",
            "",
            "Drawbars is the first",
            "page. The knobs are",
            "bars 0-7; bar 8 is",
            "further down the list."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Registrations",
          "lines": [
            "Written as the classic",
            "B3 shorthand.",
            "",
            "Jazz comp",
            " 88 8000 000",
            "",
            "Gospel",
            " 88 8800 008",
            "",
            "Full organ",
            " 88 8888 888",
            "",
            "Smooth ballad",
            " 00 8400 000",
            "",
            "Thin and reedy",
            " 00 8080 800"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Percussion",
      "lines": [
        "A single decaying tap",
        "on the attack of the",
        "first key you play.",
        "It does not retrigger",
        "until you lift every",
        "key, which is why it",
        "rewards detached",
        "playing.",
        "",
        "Perc   on or off",
        "Level  Norm or Soft",
        "Decay  Slow or Fast",
        "Harm   3rd or 2nd",
        "",
        "2nd is the bright",
        "bark. 3rd is hollow.",
        "",
        "On real hardware perc",
        "steals the 1' drawbar",
        "and thins the whole",
        "output slightly. This",
        "engine does the same.",
        "",
        "Perc only sounds on",
        "the upper manual, so",
        "on all notes here."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Vibrato",
      "lines": [
        "The B3 scanner: a",
        "mechanical delay line",
        "swept by a rotating",
        "capacitor. Not a",
        "pitch LFO.",
        "",
        "Scanner picks one of",
        "six settings.",
        "V1 V2 V3  vibrato,",
        " pitch only, shallow",
        " to deep.",
        "C1 C2 C3  chorus,",
        " dry mixed back in,",
        " which is where the",
        " shimmer comes from.",
        "",
        "Speed sets the scan",
        "rate, 4 to 22 Hz.",
        "",
        "Upper and Lower turn",
        "it on per manual.",
        "With both off the",
        "Scanner setting does",
        "nothing.",
        "",
        "C3 is the famous one."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Overdrive",
      "lines": [
        "Tube preamp stage,",
        "before the Leslie.",
        "",
        "Drive  on or off",
        "Char   0 to 1",
        "In     0 to 1",
        "Out    0 to 1",
        "",
        "Char sets the curve",
        "shape, soft to hard.",
        "In drives it. Out",
        "trims the level back",
        "down.",
        "",
        "Raising In without",
        "lowering Out will get",
        "loud fast. Default is",
        "In 0.26, Out 0.44.",
        "",
        "Drive is off by",
        "default."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Leslie and Reverb",
      "lines": [
        "Leslie",
        " Slow, Stop, Fast",
        "",
        "A rotating horn and a",
        "rotating bass drum in",
        "one cabinet. Slow is",
        "chorale, Fast is",
        "tremolo.",
        "",
        "The speed ramps. The",
        "horn and the drum",
        "have different",
        "inertia, so they",
        "drift apart on the",
        "way and lock back",
        "together. Switching",
        "mid phrase is the",
        "effect, not just a",
        "setting.",
        "",
        "Stop is the dry",
        "cabinet.",
        "",
        "Reverb  0 to 1",
        "",
        "Wet mix. 0.2 to 0.4",
        "sits behind the organ.",
        "Above 0.6 it washes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Output",
      "lines": [
        "Swell  0 to 1",
        "",
        "The expression pedal.",
        "On a B3 this is not a",
        "volume knob: it sits",
        "before the overdrive,",
        "so backing off the",
        "swell cleans the tone",
        "as well as quieting",
        "it.",
        "",
        "Default 0.8.",
        "",
        "RDY  read only",
        "",
        "0 while the engine is",
        "still building, 1 when",
        "it is ready to sound."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "MIDI",
      "lines": [
        "Notes play the upper",
        "manual. Notes outside",
        "36 to 96 fold into",
        "range by octaves,",
        "so every pad sounds.",
        "",
        "CC 11  expression,",
        " same as Swell",
        "CC 91  reverb mix",
        "CC 120 all sound off",
        "CC 123 all notes off",
        "",
        "There is no lower",
        "manual or pedalboard",
        "in this port. One",
        "keyboard, one manual.",
        "",
        "Velocity is ignored.",
        "A tonewheel organ has",
        "no velocity: the key",
        "is a set of switches,",
        "either closed or not.",
        "Use Swell for",
        "dynamics."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
